# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Elastic-net logistic regression for pulmonary embolism (PE) prediction
======================================================================

Primary validation : Harrell bootstrap optimism correction (entire pipeline repeated in every resample)
Secondary          : stratified 70:30 split
Hyper-parameters   : C and l1_ratio tuned by inner CV over prespecified grids (criterion: mean log loss)
Calibration        : Platt (sigmoid), ensemble=False -> the final model reduces to ONE closed-form equation
Comparators        : Wells and Revised Geneva scores recomputed from items using the published definitions

Usage
-----
    python pe_elasticnet_analysis.py --input data.xlsx --output results/

    # or via environment variables
    PE_INPUT=data.xlsx PE_OUTPUT=results python pe_elasticnet_analysis.py

    # smoke test (tiny number of resamples; never report these numbers)
    python pe_elasticnet_analysis.py --input data.xlsx --quick

Requirements
------------
    numpy pandas scipy statsmodels scikit-learn joblib matplotlib seaborn openpyxl
    imbalanced-learn   (optional; enables the SMOTEN arm of the repeated-CV comparison)

Input
-----
First sheet of an Excel workbook with the binary predictor columns listed in `predictor_columns`
(Yes/No or 1/0; Sex: male = 1) and the outcome column `Final Diagnosis (PTE)` (CTPA result).
Score columns already present in the workbook are NOT used; Wells and Geneva are recomputed.
"""
